      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a9de400f3791b4155afcc5b|full_name}: I came back to this canny to see if someone mentioned this exactly, because I wasn't sure if they would fire and still haven't had an opportunity to test. A bit of extra processing on that, I think: In PKCZ, the timeline objects that were calling traditional animation events and not ones made on the timeline itself hitch a little when they become active or end. \nThe most performant timeline animations we found were done on the timeline itself, though using timeline at all does seem more responsive overall than just having them as a component or gameobject. I suspect it's just perhaps threaded better.",
