  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Testing in 1121 reveals that the Signal Track/Signal Receiver feature in Timeline is non-functional in-client. This is most likely due to the Signal Receiver script not being whitelisted.\nSignal Receiver is part of Timeline's version of animation events. It was added in 2019.1.\nThis script should be whitelisted because:\n1. It's a built-in Unity script related to a major modern Unity feature.\n2. It enables equivalent functionality on (good) Timelines to allow people to move off of using (bad) extremely long animation clips.\nWhitelisting this script with the same guards as animation clips have (i.e. only being able to fire a custom event on an UdonBehaviour) makes sense. This is especially true because you can use the Activation Track feature of Timeline to switch on/off GameObjects. Then you can abuse OnEnable on a UdonBehaviour to do whatever you want.",
